#15 adds something like this to the readme:
> Bundles are loaded asynchronously, which enables other mods to do their initialization while files are being read from disk, which in turn leads to shorter startup times. **Hence, using the `.repobundle` system is the preferred way to use this library, even if you're already writing your own plugin code.**

Async bundle loading could be implemented as a part of the public API. For example:
```cs
public static class Utils
{
    public static void LoadAssetBundleAsyncBeforeLobby(string path, Action<AssetBundle> onBundleLoaded)
    {
        // Load the asset bundle async as if it were a part of the automatic async asset bundle loading system.
        // When the asset bundle is loaded, call onBundleLoaded, passing in the asset bundle.
        // This method should NOT register all the content automatically, it should only load the asset bundle.
    }
}
```
## Motivation

You simply may just want more control over loading your assets.
For example: a large mod which has multiple asset bundles which can be toggled on or off from the mod's config.

If/when this is implemented, the *"Hence, using the `.repobundle` system is the preferred way to use this library, even if you're already writing your own plugin code."* can be removed from the readme, while adding instructions for how to do it with this method.

Adds a method of registering custom chat /commands like the vanilla ones. Commands are registered by applying attributes to methods so that other mods using REPOLib can easily register their own commands. Commands can have multiple aliases by applying multiple instances of `CommandAliasAttribute`. Commands can be marked as needing developer mode (for cheat commands) and individual commands can be enabled/disabled through a config file.
Commands can also have an optional initializer method using the `CommandInitializerAttribute` attribute that gets called by `CommandManager` when it initializes. Useful for caching data needed by commands. 

Includes two commands useful for testing mods that use REPOLib: **Spawn Valuable** and **Spawn Item**. Both require the vanilla developer mode to be enabled, which can be enabled through a new config option (off by default) that patches `SteamManager`. These commands also serve as examples for others who want to make their own commands. Both commands search for valid items/valuables by name, ignoring case, and are capable of inferring the `Valuable ` or `Item ` prefixes from path names. 

For example, these are all valid forms of the same command: `/spawnvaluable Valuable Diamond`, `/spawnval diamond`, `/sv Diamond`.

Does not currently include a command for spawning enemies, as the vanilla logic for that is much more complex.

A basic chat command implementation looks like:
```cs
public static class YourCommand
{
    // ...

    [CommandInitializer]
    public static void Initialize()
    {
        // Perform any setup or caching
    }

    [CommandExecution(
        "Your Command Name",
        "Description of what the command does and how to use it.",
        enabledByDefault: true,
        requiresDeveloperMode: false,
        )]
    [CommandAlias("yourcommand")]
    [CommandAlias("yourcmd")]
    public static void Execute(string args)
    {
        // ...
    }
}
```

Note that commands can be run while in a lobby before a game actually begins, but this is also true for the vanilla commands such as `/greenscreen` so I did not include any prevention for this, for now.
